	<body bgcolor="#ffffff" text="#000000">
		<h1 class="largetext">Rodcetnife.org Forums</h1>
		<h2 class="normaltext">General Category => General Discussion => Topic started by: Rylden on March 30, 2005, 10:10:05 am</h2>

		<table width="90%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Rylden</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 10:10:05 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">From the information I have gathered it appears that it will look like this:<br /><br />1. Vis Maior<br />2. Dol Amroth/Echoes in Eternity<br />3. Wraith/Reviviscence<br />4. Conviction<br />5. Cold Fury<br />6. Moonlight Crusaders<br />7-9 Inner Loop, Union of Power, Dawning Nemesis<br />10. Outcast Adventurers<br /><br />That is based on everything I have read on both boards.  7,8, and 9 are interchangeable as I believe all are one kill away from Time.  Correct me if I&#039;m wrong.<br /><br />Let the games begin!</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Self Destruction</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 10:14:45 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Rylden $txt[176] March 30, 2005, 10:10:05 am</div><div class="quote">From the information I have gathered it appears that it will look like this:<br /><br />1. Vis Maior<br />2. Dol Amroth/Echoes in Eternity<br />3. Wraith/Revivscence<br />4. Conviction<br />5. Cold Fury<br />6. Midnight Crusaders<br />7-9. Inner Loop, Union of Power, Dawning Nemesis<br />10. Outcast Adventurers<br /></div><br /><br />Fixed..</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Qutsemnie</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 10:34:22 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Midnight crusadors is &quot;Moonlight Crusaders&quot; <br /><br />The Quellious order is correct though sorting out how they interweave is a trick =)<br />Relavent webpages in no particular order are:<br /> <br />http://www.moonlightcrusaders.com/  (Indicative Content:Finishing up learning time)<br /><br />http://reviviscence.home.comcast.net/ Which is joined in a years old raiding alliance with http://www.wraithguild.com/index1.html<br />(Officers of each are basically officers for the other when it comes to raid choices.  Its a tight bond it takes a bit of getting used to if you havent been on a server with such a tight alliance.  Very solidly out of time. They got to Time over a year ago now. Indicative Content: Tacvi South/ one MPG trial/King and Queen of RS)<br /><br />http://www.explicitguild.net/ (This is vis maior theres a bit of history in explaining why vis maiors website is explicits web site that is prolly beyond the need of this thread. This is the most hardcore of Quellious guilds.  Min raid % and all that uber jazz) Indicative Content: Somewhere in the secrets of Anguish~)<br /><br />http://www.coldfuryguild.com/ (Youll see dedication in that screen shot.  Dedication is a twink/recruit guild of cold furys. Also of relavence is they play on australia&#039;s peak time.) (Indicative Content: Ask them~  I know I have seen them in Qvic/and Queen RS with my own eyes. Though tacvi and MPG trials wouldnt surprise me.)<br /><br />-----------------------------------------------------------<br /><br />So thats all the time+ guilds.  <br />--------------------------------------------------------------<br /><br />The two most active pretime guilds are:<br />http://www.underguild.com/  (Thats the longest running elemental guild that hasnt made it to time yet.  I dont know where they stand on that)<br /><br />http://vinceremo.com/Home.htm (The most recent arrival to elemental planes just gaining entry this month not sure what their goals are)<br /><br />edit in:<br />http://www.radiantguild.org/&nbsp; (These guys were in elemental planes before Moonlight Crusaders.&nbsp;  They are rebuilding it seems.)<br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Toastie</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 10:47:10 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">fuck that, they cant just knock me off the top ten list like that...</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Rylden</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 10:48:54 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Toastie $txt[176] March 30, 2005, 10:47:10 am</div><div class="quote">fuck that, they cant just knock me off the top ten list like that...<br /></div><br /><br />Sorry, Toastie... <br /><br />1. Vis Maior<br />2. Dol Amroth/Echoes in Eternity<br />3-4. Wraith/Reviviscence, Cold Fury<br />5. Conviction<br />5.5. Toastie&#039;s Crew<br />6. Moonlight Crusaders<br />7-9. Inner Loop, Union of Power, Dawning Nemesis<br />10. Underguild<br /><br />That better?<br /><br />Cold Fury is currently reflagging for Txevu, but are Australian based so don&#039;t raid with the rest of the server.&nbsp; Which means, they are up with Wraith/Revi. unless I get something more concrete.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Gaeaan</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 11:50:25 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">The two most active pretime guilds are:<br />http://www.underguild.com/&nbsp; (Thats the longest running elemental guild that hasnt made it to time yet.&nbsp; I dont know where they stand on that)<br /></div><br /><br />Heya Rodcet.&nbsp; Leader of UG on Quellious.&nbsp; Hehe, we didn&#039;t &quot;plan&quot; on being in elementals nearly this long, but we&#039;re a firm believer in making sure everyone gets all the gear they want from content before moving on (read: we farm like we&#039;re posessed).&nbsp; We&#039;re currently working on Cor (hopefully we&#039;ll have him dead this week) and then starting up RC.&nbsp; We&#039;re fully KT flagged and also have some of the Ikky trials down.<br /><br />There&#039;s another guild on Quellious that&#039;s in ele&#039;s atm, not listed here (Radiant).&nbsp; They&#039;ve actually been in eles longer than us.&nbsp; I know they have a Fennin kill under their belts, and from what I understand, they&#039;re gonna start on Xeg and Cor soon.&nbsp; That&#039;s all just grapevine info though.<br /><br />Look forward to seeing ya&#039;ll in 6 weeks.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Grizzat</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 12:13:22 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">NOOOOO!<br /><br />We made #7 and now we aren&#039;t even in the top 10 anymore!!<br /><br />Blast!<br /><br />Oh well... that&#039;s what you get when you only raid 2 days a week.<br /><br />Yeah - Vinceremo is just entering Elemental now - our goals are slow progression cause we don&#039;t consider ourselves a raiding guild.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Rylden</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 12:42:14 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Gaeaan $txt[176] March 30, 2005, 11:50:25 am</div><div class="quote"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">The two most active pretime guilds are:<br />http://www.underguild.com/  (Thats the longest running elemental guild that hasnt made it to time yet.  I dont know where they stand on that)<br /></div><br /><br />We&#039;re currently working on Cor (hopefully we&#039;ll have him dead this week) and then starting up RC.  We&#039;re fully KT flagged and also have some of the Ikky trials down.</div><br /><br />Yeah, which places you squarely in the Ten Spot - because the three above you are one kill from time.&nbsp; Inner Loop needs Corinav and Dawning Nemesis and Union of Power only need TRC.&nbsp; It is not based on time in progression, but the most recent successful progression.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Toastie</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 01:33:06 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Rylden $txt[176] March 30, 2005, 10:48:54 am</div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Toastie $txt[176] March 30, 2005, 10:47:10 am</div><div class="quote">fuck that, they cant just knock me off the top ten list like that...<br /></div><br /><br />Sorry, Toastie... <br /><br />1. Vis Maior<br />2. Dol Amroth/Echoes in Eternity<br />3-4. Wraith/Reviviscence, Cold Fury<br />5. Conviction<br />5.5. Toastie&#039;s Crew<br />6. Moonlight Crusaders<br />7-9. Inner Loop, Union of Power, Dawning Nemesis<br />10. Underguild<br /><br />That better?<br /><br />Cold Fury is currently reflagging for Txevu, but are Australian based so don&#039;t raid with the rest of the server.&nbsp; Which means, they are up with Wraith/Revi. unless I get something more concrete.<br /></div><br /><br />i&#039;m a solid 4.5 if you ask me... but whatever works!</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Givins</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 03:07:13 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I think we need to expand to a top 15.&nbsp; When I see all these funky Quelius guild tags running around, I would like to know if it&#039;s a raiding guild or not, period.&nbsp; I&#039;d also like to sorta get the idea of exactly what the Quelious guild tags mean relative to our beloved Rodcet tags.&nbsp; But that&#039;s just my opinion.&nbsp; </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 03:12:59 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Well, if we&#039;re expanding, then I&#039;d see Radiant &amp; OA at 11&amp;12 (not sure who would be above who, both have only FR kills?), then BrewMasters at 13 with elemental access...not sure how it falls out after that... LoS would be in there somewhere, but I think there might be a Quellious guild or two between them and Brews.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Qutsemnie</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 03:30:08 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I ~almost~ changed my underguild comment of longest elemental guild not in time but i noticed right before that I said actively raiding[and radiant had a serious lull].  <br /><br />A backgrounder.  Radiant was ahead of Moonlight Crusaders once upon a time.  Entered elemental planes noticably ahead of MC.  In fact when I first joined my current guild over a year ago I got two of my pre-elemental flags on xflags with radiant.  So they were hopping.  But then sort of dried up... Ok so I looked them up for this post.  They are in a pre-elemental/early elemental rebuilding phase it looks like.<br /><br />http://www.radiantguild.org/<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Givins</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 03:35:37 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Vinceremo has just started raiding elements, I saw someone say, so they are probably #13, with our beloved Brew Masters at #14.  LOS #15?  I haven&#039;t seen anything from Q. raiding in early POP...yet...<br /><br />1. Vis Maior  (Entrenced in Aguish)<br />2. Dol Amroth/Echoes in Eternity  (Starting Anguish)<br />3-4. Wraith/Reviviscence, Cold Fury (Various stages in GoD)<br />5. Conviction (Coming out of Time, various stages of GoD)<br />6. Moonlight Crusaders (Time Farming)<br />7.&nbsp; Inner Loop (missing Coirnav)<br />8-9. Union of Power, Dawning Nemesis (missing Rathe Council)<br />10. Underguild (Perma farming Elementals)<br />11. Outcast Adventurers (Fennin Ro killed)<br />12.&nbsp; Radiant (FR kill, backflagging after lull)<br />13.  Vinceremo (Raiding elementals)<br />14.  Brew Masters (Missing Sol Ro, about to start raiding elementals)<br />15.  League of Sozobon (Flagging tier 1 mobs)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>March 30, 2005, 03:40:21 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">LoS are well past Tier 1 - they&#039;ve beaten Bertoxx and Agnarr...</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
