					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Tuladin Backbreaker - officer of Radiant<br /><br />Just to follow up on Eternalruby&#039;s post...4th FR kill tonight.&nbsp; 80% of the guild is PoEb flagged and have farmed the named there on several occasions.&nbsp; We are also ready to give Xegony a shot as well.<br /><br />Our schedual I&#039;m informed by our guildleader is 2 gods a week so expect to see us moving through the elementals in short order.<br /><br />www.radiantguild.org</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Givins</b> on <b>March 31, 2005, 03:02:04 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">1. Vis Maior  (Entrenched in Aguish)<br />2. Dol Amroth/Echoes in Eternity  (Anguish)<br />3-4. Wraith/Reviviscence, Cold Fury (Various stages in GoD)<br />5. Conviction (Coming out of Time, various stages of GoD)<br />6. Moonlight Crusaders (Time Farming)<br />7.  Inner Loop (missing Coirnav)<br />8-9. Union of Power, Dawning Nemesis (missing Rathe Council)<br />10. Underguild (FR and Xegony killed)<br />11. Radiant (FR kill, Poe B)<br />12.  Outcast Adventurers (Fennin Ro killed)<br />13.  Brew Masters (Killed Sol Ro, about to start raiding elementals)<br />14.  Vinceremo (Missing Sol Ro)<br />15.  League of Sozobon (kill Agnar and Bert)<br /><br />Edit:&nbsp; Moved BM up to #13 and Vinceremo to #14.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Atlis</b> on <b>March 31, 2005, 05:37:19 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">On Quellious you&#039;ve also got the special case of ORQ.&nbsp; An entity which generally raids Tier 1 and Tier 2 PoP, as well as many other targets.&nbsp; ORQ is the small-guild / non-guild collection which gathers for a purpose.&nbsp; It&#039;s not quite pickup, but not quite guild.<br />In the past, there was also URoN, the elemental raiding version of ORQ.&nbsp; That group has dissolved after WoW/EQ2, however, ORQ is still strong.<br /><br />How or would you categorize a non-guild organization?<br /><br />This is also informing all on Rodcet that Quellious is often game for nontraditional raid entities.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>March 31, 2005, 06:04:49 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Givins - Brews have killed both Sol Ro and RZtW</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>xaanru</b> on <b>March 31, 2005, 08:16:27 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">[How or would you categorize a non-guild organization?<br />/quote]<br /><br />Since this is a top 10 (15 now) GUILDS list, I&#039;d say not at all. That would be like saying how do you classify all the unguilded people who are flagged for elementals, and COULD conceivably band together for a raid.<br /><br />If there is a formal alliance, that is progressing, it will be listed like DA/EiE. Plus, tier 1 and 2 mobs would put them solidly somewhere below the 15 spot anyhow.</div></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
