					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Honestly, I tihnk Ikkinz 3 is a bit trickier than Ikkinz 4 was. We generally had alot less problems with that one (Ikkinz 4) for some odd reason. Once we worked out a method that worked a bit better for us in 3 it got easier too, of course by that time it mighta also been the levels too. Who knows, but gratz none the less.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Toastie</b> on <b>May 23, 2005, 04:24:39 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">for a long time, ikkinz 4 was all about luck with the final mob and how many adds spawned, and what types...<br /><br />i&#039;ve probably done that instance 30-40 times and it was always interesting to see what exactly we&#039;d be handed.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Top Ten Quellious/Rodcet Nife Guilds</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Prodigy</b> on <b>May 23, 2005, 05:08:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I think it&#039;s safe to say Keeper of the Altar is &quot;OMFG BURN HIM&quot;<br /><br />&quot;GD someone kite the F**** ADDS!!&quot;<br /><br />Was fun as hell.&nbsp; We had 48 in zone when he was around 15%.&nbsp; But then another 10-15 dropped off right at the end :( I think we got 30 flags or so.&nbsp;  <br /><br />Ikkinz 3 is easy once you learn how to single those last mobs out.<br /><br />I&#039;m just not looking forward to Ugua.&nbsp; <br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
